{"id":"swh-t1-0002","lang":"swh","tier":1,"slot":"count.five","domain":2,"text_native":"Tano","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Five.","source_caption":"Five.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Five is where most of these languages change to a different counting pattern, and knowing that in advance is the point of learning them in order.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Swahili phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Swahili","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
